.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * 
. 
. * We conduct our analysis running panel data fixed effects at the household l
> evel 
. * Our dependent variable is the percertage of housework by men in the housego
> ld (phmen)
. * The set of independent variable includes age, age2, level ofd education, pe
> rcentage of
. * net labor income earned by husband, employment status (dummies for full-tim
> e), total 
. * number of hours devoted to housework in the household (housework_cid) and y
> ear dummies 
. * We include fixed effects at the household level (cid)
. 
.         xtset cid syear

Panel variable: cid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2009 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg phmale d_daughter age age2 age_partner age_partner_2 pgisced11 
> edu_partner share_income fulltime full_partner housework_cid  i.syear , fe cl
> uster(cid)
note: 2019.syear omitted because of collinearity.

Fixed-effects (within) regression               Number of obs     =        951
